<!-- 3. THE HOOK (R-STACK) -->
<section>
    <h2>The Big Question</h2>
    <div class="r-stack">
        <div class="fragment fade-in-then-out">
            <div class="question-box">
                <p style="font-size:1.25em;">🤔 If an algorithm makes a decision…</p>
                <p style="font-size:1.25em; margin-top:0.6em;">is it automatically <strong>fair</strong>?</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fragment fade-in-then-out">
            <div class="box" style="background:#ffebee;">
                <p style="font-size:1.15em;"><strong>❌ Common misconception:</strong> “Algorithms are neutral.”</p>
                <p class="small-text">Models learn from historical data — including human bias.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fragment fade-in">
            <div class="box-blue">
                <p style="font-size:1.15em;"><strong>✅ Reality:</strong> ML systems can amplify bias, invade privacy, and shift responsibility.</p>
                <p class="small-text">Ethics asks what we <em>should</em> do with this power.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 4. KEY ETHICAL THEMES -->
<section>
    <h3>Core ethical issues in machine learning</h3>
    <div class="question-box">What can go wrong when ML decisions affect real lives?</div>
    <div class="cols">
        <div class="box">
            <p class="fragment"><span class="keyword" data-def="Who is responsible for decisions made with/through ML systems.">Accountability</span> — who is responsible?</p>
            <p class="fragment"><span class="keyword" data-def="Systematic unfairness caused by biased data, design choices, or deployment context.">Bias</span> &amp; <span class="keyword" data-def="Ethical goal that model outcomes do not discriminate unjustly against groups.">fairness</span> — are outcomes equitable?</p>
            <p class="fragment"><span class="keyword" data-def="Permission for data to be collected/used for a specific purpose.">Consent</span> — did people agree to data use?</p>
            <p class="fragment"><span class="keyword" data-def="Protection of personal information from misuse or unwanted exposure.">Privacy</span> — can data be misused?</p>
            <p class="fragment"><span class="keyword" data-def="Energy use and carbon emissions from training and running ML systems.">Environmental impact</span> — energy and carbon cost</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box-blue">
            <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i> A common pattern</h4>
            <p class="small-text fragment">Small design choices (data sources, labels, thresholds) can create large social effects.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 5. ACCOUNTABILITY -->
<section>
    <h3>Accountability</h3>
    <div class="question-box">If a self-driving car causes harm, who is responsible?</div>
    <div class="box">
        <p class="fragment">Accountability can be shared across designers, deployers, and operators.</p>
        <p class="fragment">Ethical systems need clear responsibility, auditing, and governance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box-blue">
        <p class="small-text"><strong>Practical safeguards:</strong> logging, monitoring, human override, and transparent decision processes.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 6. BIAS & FAIRNESS -->
<section>
    <h3>Bias &amp; fairness</h3>
    <div class="question-box">How can “learning from data” reproduce discrimination?</div>
    <div class="cols">
        <div class="box">
            <p class="fragment">Biased training data → biased predictions.</p>
            <p class="fragment">Some groups may be under-represented or mislabelled.</p>
            <p class="fragment">Fairness often requires active measurement and mitigation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box-red">
            <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> Real-world examples</h4>
            <p class="small-text fragment">Hiring tools that disadvantage women; risk-scoring tools that show racial bias.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box">
        <p><strong>Mitigations:</strong> diverse datasets, bias audits, fairness metrics, and human review for high-stakes decisions.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 7. QUICK CHECK (BIAS) -->
<section data-background="#fff3e0">
    <h3>🧠 Quick Check</h3>
    <div class="box">
        <p class="fragment">A facial recognition system has a higher false-positive rate for one demographic group.</p>
        <p class="fragment"><strong>Identify</strong> the ethical issue and <strong>outline</strong> one mitigation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box-blue">
        <p><strong>Issue:</strong> algorithmic bias / unfairness across groups.</p>
        <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong> improve training data balance + evaluate performance per group + adjust thresholds / add human review.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 7. CONSENT & PRIVACY -->
<section>
    <h3>Consent &amp; privacy</h3>
    <div class="question-box">Can you do ML on data just because you have it?</div>
    <div class="cols">
        <div class="box">
            <p class="fragment"><strong>Consent:</strong> people should understand and agree to how data is used.</p>
            <p class="fragment"><strong>Privacy risks:</strong> identifying individuals, inferring sensitive traits, data leaks.</p>
            <p class="fragment"><strong>Surveillance:</strong> ML can scale monitoring (faces, movement, behaviour).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box-blue">
            <h4>Design choices</h4>
            <p class="small-text fragment">Minimize data collection (data minimization).</p>
            <p class="small-text fragment">Use anonymization/pseudonymization where appropriate.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box">
        <p><strong>🔗 Connection to A2:</strong> network security protects the data pipelines ML depends on.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 8. ENVIRONMENTAL IMPACT -->
<section>
    <h3>Environmental impact</h3>
    <div class="question-box">What is the cost of training large models?</div>
    <div class="box">
        <p class="fragment">Training and serving large models consumes significant electricity and hardware resources.</p>
        <p class="fragment">This creates carbon emissions and e-waste concerns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box-blue">
        <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong> efficient models, responsible scaling, green data centres, and reusing models via transfer learning.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 9. QUICK CHECK -->
<section data-background="#fff3e0">
    <h3>🧠 Quick Check</h3>
    <div class="box">
        <p class="fragment">A company uses ML to screen job applications.</p>
        <p class="fragment"><strong>Discuss</strong> two ethical risks and one mitigation for each.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box-blue">
        <p><strong>Risk 1:</strong> bias against groups due to historical hiring data → mitigation: bias audit + diverse training data + human review.</p>
        <p><strong>Risk 2:</strong> privacy/consent issues from scraping applicant data → mitigation: transparent consent policies + data minimization.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 10. MISCONCEPTION CHECK -->
<section>
    <h3>Misconception Check</h3>
    <div class="question-box">True or False: “If a model is accurate, it must be fair.”</div>
    <div class="fragment box-red">
        <p><strong>False.</strong> A model can be highly accurate overall while still producing unfair outcomes for particular groups.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fragment box">
        <p>Fairness is a separate question from accuracy — and depends on context and impact.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- 11. SUMMARY -->
<section data-background="linear-gradient(135deg, #0E214B 0%, #1a3a7a 100%)">
    <h2 style="color:white;">Key Takeaways</h2>
    <div class="box" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); color:white;">
        <ul style="line-height:1.5;">
            <li>Ethics in ML includes accountability, bias/fairness, consent, privacy, and environmental impact.</li>
            <li>ML systems can amplify existing inequalities if trained on biased data.</li>
            <li>High-stakes decisions need transparency, auditing, and human oversight.</li>
            <li>Responsible ML balances performance with people’s rights and societal impact.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="box" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); color:white;">
        <p><strong>Connection:</strong> Ethical design is part of “good engineering” — not an optional extra.</p>
    </div>
</section>
